{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["<b>You shall take no ransom for the life of a murderer.</b> Scripture declares that he shall not be released for any money in the world, because the sin of murder has no equal among all the transgressions between a person and his fellow. And Scripture says (Proverbs 28:17): ״אדם עשוק בדם נפש עד בור ינוס אל יתמכו בו״. Go forth and learn from Ahab, for it is said (I Kings 22): ״רק לא היה כאבאב״ — only there was none like Ahab — and when his sins and merits were weighed before the Holy One, blessed be He, no sin was found in him to obligate destruction and to prosecute against him at first except for Naboth, as it is written (I Kings 22): ״ותצא הרוח מלפני ה׳״, and our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted: this is the spirit of Naboth; and it is written (ibid.): ״ויאמר לו תפתה וגם תוכל צא ועשה כן״, and that wicked man did not kill him with his own hands but only caused his killing — all the more so for one who kills with his own hand."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:38:01.366237175Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}